# What stays OUT of the knowledge graph (`graphify-out/`).
#
# Syntax is `.gitignore` syntax, and graphify reads this file AFTER `.gitignore`
# — so it can only ever exclude MORE, never re-include something `.gitignore`
# already dropped. Adding a line here is safe in exactly one direction: the
# graph gets narrower, never wider.
#
# `bun run graph:artifacts:check` enforces the entries below that are plain
# paths or directories: a rebuild that ran without this file re-admits what was
# excluded here, and that gate is what catches it. Glob patterns are REPORTED as
# unenforced rather than silently skipped — an exclusion that looks guarded and
# is not is worse than one that is plainly manual.
#
# Read `docs/awcms/knowledge-graph.md` before adding an entry. Exclusion is
# content the graph will no longer be able to answer from, so the bar is a
# measured one: does this path restate something already indexed, or form a blob
# that connects only to itself?

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Translation mirrors (`*.id.md`) — the source is indexed, not both halves.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# ADR-0097 makes English at the bare path the source and Indonesian at
# `<name>.id.md` a mirror that records the hash of the English it was translated
# from. A mirror therefore RESTATES its source word for word, in another
# language. Indexing both puts every concept into the graph twice, and the
# second copy contributes no sentence the first did not.
#
# This is not a hypothetical cost. When this file was written the corpus held
# 260 tracked `*.id.md` files and the last graph had scanned only 4 of them —
# because 256 of them (`.claude/skills/**/SKILL.id.md`) landed on 2026-08-15 in
# commit 01c06f39, AFTER that graph was built. So the exclusion reads as
# near-free against today's artifact (8 nodes, 0.08%) while actually preventing
# 256 restatements from entering on the next rebuild.
#
# The failure mode is specific, not merely bloat. A pair of documents with
# identical content clusters into two adjacent, nearly indistinguishable
# communities, and the automatic hub namer gives both the same name — which is
# precisely what `graph:artifacts:check` rejects ("no two communities share a
# name"). Without this line the first wave of mirrors would turn that gate red
# on the next rebuild, for a reason that has nothing to do with the code.
#
# Nothing is lost: every mirror's source is indexed, and `bun run
# check:docs:translation` already guards that the mirrors stay current.
#
# This is a GLOB, so the gate reports it as UNENFORCED rather than checking it.
# That is the correct state to print, not to hide.
*.id.md

